c64-x25519 — vendored library provenance
==========================================

upstream:       https://github.com/JC-000/c64-x25519
version:        <release tag you vendored, e.g. v0.13.0>
commit:         <SHA from `git rev-parse HEAD` at release tag>
tag:            <the same release tag, e.g. v0.13.0>
tarball_sha256: <sha256sum of the release tarball>
date_imported:  <ISO 8601 date the downstream consumer imported this>

license:        MIT
license_file:   LICENSE
release_notes:  https://github.com/JC-000/c64-x25519/releases/tag/<the same release tag>

local_modifications: none
    (if patched, list patches as "patches/000N-description.patch" below)

build_toolchain:
    ca65:       cc65 v2.x or newer (cc65.github.io)
    ld65:       cc65 v2.x or newer
    ar65:       cc65 v2.x or newer
    vice:       required only for running the upstream test suite

system_requirements:
    platform:   Commodore 64 (stock 6502)
    ram:        BASIC ROM banked out; library owns $14-$16, $1C, $1E-$2A,
                $2C-$2F and $40-$7F ZP while running — 85 bytes, the value
                of the published equate LIB_X25519_ZP_USAGE_BYTES. $FB-$FE
                is test-harness scratch only and is explicitly NOT part of
                the library's claimed ZP surface; do not reserve it.
    reu:        depends on the build profile. The DEFAULT build requires a
                512 KB REU (1750 or compatible — a window of at least 6
                banks of 64 KB). lib-x25519-1764 lowers this to 256 KB.
                lib-x25519-onchip requires NO REU at all: that profile
                issues no REU traffic and runs on a stock expansion-less
                C64. Do not record "REQUIRED" without naming the profile.
    banks_used: the published equate LIB_X25519_REU_BANKS_USED, a bitmask
                of banks claimed for the mul tables (shifted by
                X25519_REU_BANK). Default $3B = banks 0, 1, 3, 4, 5 —
                FIVE banks, 320 KB of tables. lib-x25519-1764 $03 =
                banks 0, 1 (128 KB). lib-x25519-onchip $00 = none.
                Bank 2 lies inside the window but is never claimed in any
                configuration (the legacy zero stash was removed in v0.6
                prep). See docs/LIBRARY.md §7 for the full memory map.

public_api:     see src/x25519.inc for the machine-readable header
integration:    see docs/LIBRARY.md §4 for step-by-step vendoring guide

